# Deploy Conventions

## Docker Compose Services

| Service | Image | Port | Depends On |
|---------|-------|------|------------|
| mysql | mysql:8.0 | 3307 | — |
| openfga-migrate | alpine:3.19 | — | mysql |
| openfga | openfga/openfga:v1.5.3 | 8180, 8181, 3001 | mysql, openfga-migrate |
| openfga-init | alpine:3.19 | — | openfga |
| clickhouse | clickhouse-server:24.8 | 8123, 9000 | — |
| clickhouse-init | clickhouse-server:24.8 | — | clickhouse |
| otel-collector | otel-collector-contrib:0.137.0 | 4317, 4318, 8888, 13133 | clickhouse |
| vector | Build `../vector/` | 8686, 14317, 14318 | — | *(commented out in `docker-compose.yml` by default; uncomment the service block and set `VECTOR_ENABLED=true` in `.env` to enable)* |
| pulse-ui | Build `pulse-ui/` | 3000 | pulse-server |
| pulse-server | Build `backend/server/` | 8080 | mysql, clickhouse, openfga, pulse-ai-agent |
| pulse-ai-agent | Build `pulse_ai/` | 8000 | — |
| pulse-alerts-cron | Build `backend/pulse-alerts-cron/` | 4000 | mysql, pulse-server, clickhouse |

**Pulse AI:** `pulse-ai-agent` is part of the default deploy stack (`docker compose up`). Set `GOOGLE_API_KEY` in `deploy/.env` for Gemini; the process starts without it but model/API calls fail. **Standalone** AI-only dev: `pulse_ai/docker-compose.yml` + `cd pulse_ai && ./setup.sh [start|stop|restart|logs|clean]`.

## Network

All services on `pulse-network` (bridge). Internal references use container names (e.g., `mysql`, `clickhouse:8123`, `openfga:8080`).

## Volumes

`mysql-data`, `clickhouse-data` — persistent. Use `./scripts/reset-databases.sh` to wipe. `vector-data` is declared in compose but only used when the Vector service block is uncommented.

## Environment Variables

- `APP_ENVIRONMENT` — **Required.** Application environment (`dev`, `stag`, `uat`, `prod`). Validated at startup. Passed to pulse-server in docker-compose (default: `dev`).
- `CONFIG_SERVICE_APPLICATION_*` — backend app config
- `CONFIG_REPLAY_API_BASE_URL` — session replay API base URL (e.g. `http://localhost:3400`); used in default SDK config
- `VAULT_SERVICE_*` — secrets (Slack, Grafana, etc.)
- `OTEL_CLICKHOUSE_*` — OTEL collector ClickHouse connection
- `REACT_APP_*` — frontend build-time config
- `NOTIFICATION_*` — notification service (SQS queue URLs, retry, worker tuning)
- `SES_*` — Amazon SES email config
- `SLACK_*` — Slack OAuth integration (client ID, secret, scopes, redirect URI, UI redirect URL)
- `OPENFGA_*` — OpenFGA authorization service config
- `AWS_*` — AWS credentials for Athena/S3
- `COMPOSE_PROFILES` — Optional. Used for Vector (`VECTOR_ENABLED=true` appends `vector`). Plain `docker compose` also reads this env when set manually.
- `GOOGLE_API_KEY` — Google GenAI / ADK for `pulse-ai-agent` (process starts without it; Gemini calls fail at runtime).
- `PULSE_BASE_URL` — Base URL for pulse_ai tools → pulse-server (compose default: `http://pulse-server:8080`).
- `SESSION_DB_URL` — AI session DB; compose defaults to SQLite on volume `pulse-ai-sessions`.
- `AI_SERVICE_URL` — URL pulse-server uses for AI proxy (compose default: `http://pulse-ai-agent:8000`). Override (e.g. `http://host.docker.internal:8000`) when AI runs on the host or outside deploy compose.
- `SPAN_COLLECTOR_URL` — OTLP span collector endpoint (default: `http://localhost:4318/v1/traces`)
- `LOGS_COLLECTOR_URL` — OTLP logs collector endpoint (default: `http://localhost:4318/v1/logs`)
- `METRIC_COLLECTOR_URL` — OTLP metrics collector endpoint (default: `http://localhost:4318/v1/metrics`)
- `CUSTOM_EVENT_COLLECTOR_URL` — Custom event collector endpoint (default: `http://localhost:4318/v1/logs`)
- `INTERACTION_CONFIG_URL` — Interaction config URL (default: `http://localhost:4318/v1/traces`)
- `VECTOR_ENABLED` — Optional. Set to `true` when using Vector (custom events → S3/Athena). The Vector **service is commented out** in `docker-compose.yml` until you uncomment it. Default: `false`.

**Dev Mode Configuration:**
- `GOOGLE_OAUTH_ENABLED` — Enable/disable Google OAuth login (default: `false` for dev mode)
- `DEV_MODE_API_KEY` — Hardcoded API key for default-project when OAuth is disabled (default: `default-project_devkey01`). Format: `{projectId}_{suffix}` (single underscore for project ID extraction).

Credentials (defined in docker-compose, overridable via `.env`):
- MySQL: `MYSQL_USER` / `MYSQL_PASSWORD` (defaults: `pulse_user` / `pulse_password`)
- ClickHouse: `OTEL_CLICKHOUSE_USER` / `OTEL_CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD` (defaults: `pulse_user` / `pulse_password`)
- ClickHouse Cluster: `CLICKHOUSE_CLUSTER_NAME` — Passed to pulse-server in docker-compose. Use empty string for single-node (local dev). Must be non-blank in `prod`.
- OpenFGA: `OPENFGA_STORE_ID` / `OPENFGA_MODEL_ID` (generated by init script)

## Scripts

| Script | Options |
|--------|---------|
| `build.sh` | `[--no-cache]` and targets `ui`, `server`, `cron`, `ai`, `all` — default / `all` includes `pulse-ai-agent` |
| `start.sh` | `[-d` or `--detach] [--build] [--no-cache] [--skip-env-check]` |
| `stop.sh` | `-v` to remove volumes; service aliases include `ai`, `pulse-ai-agent` |
| `logs.sh` | service name (e.g., `server`, `ai`, `otel-collector`) |
| `quickstart.sh` | `[--no-cache] [--skip-env-check]` — builds + starts stack (includes AI) |
| `reset-databases.sh` | drops volumes and reinitializes |
| `init-clickhouse.sh` | creates ClickHouse tables from schema SQL + session-summary MV |

**Env validation:** `quickstart.sh` and `start.sh` validate `.env` against `docker-compose.yml`: **required** = variables in compose with no default (`${VAR}`); missing in `.env` → error. **Optional** = variables with a default in compose (`${VAR:-...}`); missing in `.env` → warning (compose uses default). No auto-copy from `.env.example`; only required keys must be set. Collector/config URL vars must be valid `http://` or `https://` URLs. Use `--skip-env-check` to skip. The parser in `deploy/scripts/common.sh` retains the last line even when `.env` has no trailing newline (e.g. pasted tokens).

**Required (no default in compose):** `VAULT_ENCRYPTION_MASTER_KEY`, `REACT_APP_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`, `REACT_APP_FIREBASE_*`, `CONFIG_SERVICE_APPLICATION_GOOGLEOAUTHCLIENTID`, `CONFIG_SERVICE_APPLICATION_GCP_PROJECT_ID`, `CONFIG_SERVICE_APPLICATION_WEBHOOKURL`, `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` / `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` / `AWS_SESSION_TOKEN`. Must be set in `.env`. `SLACK_*` are optional (default empty; needed only for Slack API integration).

**Cursor config audit:** Service list and env rules match `deploy/docker-compose.yml`. Vector is optional: uncomment its service in compose and set `VECTOR_ENABLED=true` in `.env`.
